- Exactly.

277
00:16:31,426 --> 00:16:33,417
- 前驱只适合弱者。
- 扯淡。
- And front-wheel drive is for the feeble.
- No.

278
00:16:33,495 --> 00:16:34,985
- 这车是后驱。
- 我清楚。
- This is rear-wheel drive.
- I know.

279
00:16:35,063 --> 00:16:37,497
- 有赛车血统。
- 这东西…想想吧。
- Racing pedigree.
- This piece... Think about it.

280
00:16:37,565 --> 00:16:39,260
- …是为了让 Alfa 再次光彩照人。
...is to make Alfa look good again.

281
00:16:39,334 --> 00:16:43,862
这…我刚才说的…这就是…
全黑的，它是一首邪恶的交响曲。
This, as I just... This is...
In black, this is a symphony of evil.

282
00:16:43,938 --> 00:16:45,769
- 不是黑的，是灰的。
- 是黑的。
- It's not black, it's gray.
- It's black.

283
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:47,273
- 那是什么？
- 那是… 什么？
- What's that?
- It's a... What?

284
00:16:47,342 --> 00:16:49,401
- 那是什么？
- 鸟屎。
- What's that?
- Bird dirt.

285
00:16:49,477 --> 00:16:52,640
我觉得你的车，
是外形炫耀却毫无内涵的试验。
Yours is, I think,
a trial of style over substance.

286
00:16:52,714 --> 00:16:55,080
我甚至不敢看
这车的前脸
I can't even look at the front
of one of these cars

287
00:16:55,150 --> 00:16:57,482
因为会让我产生……性冲动。
because I get sexually excited.

288
00:16:59,487 --> 00:17:03,480
谢天谢地，杰里米的话
被哈蒙德的出现打断了。
Mercifully, Jeremy was
interrupted by the arrival of Hammond.

289
00:17:03,558 --> 00:17:06,891
- 达斯汀·霍夫曼来了。
- 你好啊。
- Dustin Hoffmond has arrived.
- Hello, there.

290
00:17:06,961 --> 00:17:09,896
- 那是…
- 看呐……斯帕伊德（Spider）。
- That's...
- Behold... the Spider.

291
00:17:10,698 --> 00:17:13,462
- 我早就料到你会买斯帕伊德。
- 我早就料到他会。
- I knew you'd buy a Spider.
- I knew he would.

292
00:17:13,535 --> 00:17:16,402
这是仅配有
一个挡风玻璃刮水器的版本。
This is the version
that only had one windscreen wiper.

293
00:17:16,471 --> 00:17:19,565
- 不，其实还有另一个。
- 像西罗科（Scirocco）一样。
- No, actually, there is another.
- Like a Scirocco.

294
00:17:19,641 --> 00:17:22,474
这就是典型的
小型意大利跑车。
This is the definitive
small Italian sports car.

295
00:17:22,544 --> 00:17:25,445
我简直不敢相信
你能花一千英镑买到这种车。
I couldn't believe you can get one of these
for a grand.

296
00:17:25,513 --> 00:17:28,949
- 你知道我们应该…
- 那不一定管用。
- You know we're supposed to be...
- That doesn't always work.

297
00:17:29,017 --> 00:17:30,644
- 完全没用。
- 不。
- It doesn't work at all.
- No.

298
00:17:30,718 --> 00:17:31,685
我们从这里开始吧。
Let's start here.

299
00:17:31,753 --> 00:17:33,380
- 车门的后视镜能用吗？
- 不能。
- Does the door mirror work?
- No.

300
00:17:33,455 --> 00:17:34,854
- 这扇窗能开吗？
- 不能。
- Does this window work?
- No.

301
00:17:34,923 --> 00:17:36,584
- 那些开关有用了么？
- 真的一点也没有。
- Any of those switches?
- Not really, no.

302
00:17:36,658 --> 00:17:37,955
- 没有。那窗户？
- 没有。
- No. That window?
- No.

303
00:17:38,026 --> 00:17:39,755
- 那个挡风玻璃刮水器？
- 不能。
- That windscreen wiper?
- No.

304
00:17:39,828 --> 00:17:43,696
- 至少方向盘没有晃动。
- 这都是它的……特色所在。
- At least there's no play in the steering.
- That's all part of the character of...

305
00:17:43,765 --> 00:17:46,063
各位观众，请看看前轮。
Have a look at the front wheels,
ladies and gentlemen.

306
00:17:46,134 --> 00:17:48,125
你可以把这车
开进美国大片里。
You could drive this
through an American movie.

307
00:17:48,203 --> 00:17:50,728
我们本可以吵到
下周中旬才停下来
We could have bickered
until the middle of next week

308
00:17:50,805 --> 00:17:53,740
但制作组，
想把我们搞成蠢材，
but the producers,
keen to show we were morons,

309
00:17:53,808 --> 00:17:56,606
已经准备好给我们第一个挑战了。
were ready with the first challenge.

310
00:17:56,678 --> 00:18:01,581
“早在1743年，阿尔法·罗密欧
的确是个成功的赛车队。”
"Back in 1743, Alfa Romeo
was indeed a successful racing team."

311
00:18:02,450 --> 00:18:04,475
看吧，他们根本不懂这个点子。
See, they haven't got the idea of this at all.

312
00:18:04,552 --> 00:18:08,215
“现在我们要看看
那段赛车血统还剩多少。”
"We shall now see how much
of that racing pedigree has survived.

313
00:18:08,289 --> 00:18:11,986
“于是你们将去
罗金厄姆赛道进行跑道日…”
"You will therefore go to a track day
at Rockingham race circuit..."

314
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:16,292
- 哦，我没料到会这样。
- 这次你也没预料到吧。
- Ooh. I hadn't seen that one coming.
- You haven't seen this one coming, either.

315
00:18:16,364 --> 00:18:19,959
“…每超一辆车，你会得到一分”
每超一辆车。
"...where you will get one point
for every car you overtake

316
00:18:20,034 --> 00:18:23,902
每被超一次，
就会扣一分。
"and lose one
every time you are overtaken."

317
00:18:26,341 --> 00:18:28,901
- 哈。
- 我可能会让你惊讶。
- Ah.
- I may surprise you.

318
00:18:28,977 --> 00:18:30,808
但我打赌，我不会。
I bet you I don't, though.

319
00:18:30,879 --> 00:18:32,540
- 好的。
- 出发吧。
- Right.
- Let's go.

320
00:18:32,614 --> 00:18:35,242
我们上马
奔向罗金厄姆。
We saddled up
and headed for Rockingham.

321
00:18:36,718 --> 00:18:38,049
好啊，咱们俩都干了。
Well, two of us did.

322
00:18:38,119 --> 00:18:40,917
这事儿不可能顺顺利利的。
It won't work in a smooth way.

323
00:18:44,092 --> 00:18:46,458
跑道日的概念其实很简单——
The idea of a track day
is very simple -

324
00:18:46,528 --> 00:18:48,496
任何人都能开着任何车出现
anyone can turn up with any car

325
00:18:48,563 --> 00:18:52,727
然后尽可能快地把它冲起来，玩上一会儿。
and spend some time blasting it around
as fast as possible.

326
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:55,894
这弯儿要特别注意负荷啊。
Be very conscious of the loading,
especially on this corner.

327
00:18:55,970 --> 00:18:58,097
当然，先来了个安全简报。
Naturally, there was a safety briefing

328
00:18:58,172 --> 00:19:01,141
不过，多亏了詹姆斯，我们迟到了点儿。
but, thanks to James, we arrived a bit late.

329
00:19:01,209 --> 00:19:02,972
...坚持你的线路...
- 抱歉。
...stick to your line...
- Sorry.

330
00:19:03,044 --> 00:19:04,602
- 抱歉，各位。
- 下午好。
- Sorry, everyone.
- Afternoon.

331
00:19:04,679 --> 00:19:06,146
- 抱歉。
- 是他不好。
- Sorry.
- It was his fault.

332
00:19:06,214 --> 00:19:11,117
好，左边或右边都行。坚持你的线，让超车的车儿过去。
OK, overtake either side. Stick to your line
and let the overtaking car get past you.

333
00:19:11,185 --> 00:19:12,379
行了，大家满意了吧？
OK. Everybody happy?

334
00:19:13,688 --> 00:19:14,814
好，好。
Good, good.

335
00:19:14,889 --> 00:19:18,017
- 第一段是啥？
- 我觉得我们漏了不少。
- What was the first bit?
- I think we may have missed quite a lot.

336
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:22,489
不过，绕着跑道开车——能有多难？
Still, driving round a track -
how hard can it be?

337
00:19:22,564 --> 00:19:25,294
- 哈蒙德，我要贴着你后面走。
- 好的。
- Hammond, I'm gonna stick behind you.
- OK.

338
00:19:25,366 --> 00:19:27,630
然后我在直道上抢你一杆，拿个积分。
Then I'm gonna take you on the straight
and get a point.

339
00:19:27,702 --> 00:19:28,760
别指望了。
I don't think so.

340
00:19:28,836 --> 00:19:31,304
- 你这车有多少马力？
- 126。
- How many horsepower have you got?
- 126.

341
00:19:31,372 --> 00:19:34,170
- 190。
- 它们全坏了，只有三条腿。
- 190.
- They're all broken. They've got three legs.

342
00:19:34,242 --> 00:19:38,201
右，右，左，左，左，右...左，右，左。
Right, right, left, left, left, right...
left, right, left.

343
00:19:39,447 --> 00:19:40,607
直走。
Straight.

344
00:19:42,116 --> 00:19:44,914
哎呀！听这声音。
Ohh! Listen to that.

345
00:19:46,621 --> 00:19:49,351
在赛道上我们被吓了一跳。
0n the circuit
we got a bit of a shock.

346
00:19:51,426 --> 00:19:52,688
我已经掉一格了。
I'm minus one already.

347
00:19:54,596 --> 00:19:55,688
他妈的。
Bloody hell.

348
00:19:58,633 --> 00:20:00,328
一圈下来直接掉了三格。
That's minus three in one lap.

349
00:20:02,270 --> 00:20:04,431
詹姆斯和杰里米的情况已经够糟了
Things were bad
for James and Jeremy

350
00:20:04,505 --> 00:20:06,166
但对我来说更惨。
but they were worse for me.

351
00:20:09,077 --> 00:20:09,873
啥！？
What?!

352
00:20:11,079 --> 00:20:12,068
啊——！
Aghhh!

353
00:20:13,147 --> 00:20:16,639
三圈下来一点都没超车，
After three laps
of not overtaking a single thing,

354
00:20:16,718 --> 00:20:18,879
我们只好溜回维修站。
we scuttled back to the pits.

355
00:20:19,821 --> 00:20:20,788
抱歉。
Sorry.

356
00:20:20,855 --> 00:20:22,948
这下，我终于明白了。
And there, the penny dropped.

357
00:20:23,324 --> 00:20:26,691
保时捷911，还有一台GT3 RS。
Porsche 911, another GT3 RS.

358
00:20:26,761 --> 00:20:29,628
- 莲花Elise，保时捷…
- 保时捷。
- Lotus Elise, Porsche...
- Porsche.

359
00:20:29,697 --> 00:20:31,187
保时捷。
Porsche.

360
00:20:31,265 --> 00:20:34,234
我还以为跑道日只给那些小子玩儿……
I thought track days
were just for yobbos in...

361
00:20:34,302 --> 00:20:35,394
- Saxos.  
- 是啊。
- Saxos.
- Yeah.

362
00:20:35,470 --> 00:20:40,203
显然我们得想办法让对手慢下来。
Plainly, we had to think of
a way of slowing the opposition down.

363
00:20:40,274 --> 00:20:42,606
伙计们，我有点子。吓他们一跳。
Guys, I've got an idea. Unnerve them.

364
00:20:43,311 --> 00:20:45,176
- 早上好。那是什么？  
- 五号。
- Morning. What's that?
- A five.

365
00:20:45,246 --> 00:20:48,511
是五号吗？他们不是之前那个方向盘有问题的那批吗，
It's a five? They're the ones
that had the steering issues, didn't they,

366
00:20:48,583 --> 00:20:51,552
- 那时候你开得很快？  
- 那其实…
- when you were going really fast?
- Well, it actually...

367
00:20:51,619 --> 00:20:54,747
不过你记不记得，你飞快的时候，那车常卡住？
But d'you remember, when you went
really quick, how they used to jam?

368
00:20:54,822 --> 00:20:56,653
- 哦，是的。  
- 对，的确卡住了。
- Oh, yeah.
- Yeah, they did.

369
00:20:56,991 --> 00:20:58,822
你有没有遇到过那种…的问题？
Have you had
any of the problems with the...

370
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:02,996
几年前他们一直在说的发动机舱起火的事，你有遇到过吗？
with the engine-compartment fire thing
that they went on about a few years ago?

371
00:21:03,064 --> 00:21:05,794
- 这哪里听来的？  
- 我们在《Top Gear》赛道上遇到过。
- Where did you hear that?
- We had it at Top Gear, on the track.

372
00:21:05,867 --> 00:21:07,858
跟硬弯有关吧。
Something to do with hard cornering.

373
00:21:07,935 --> 00:21:10,665
A GT2？就是那批，碟刹以前会…
A GT2? They were the ones,
the discs used to...

374
00:21:10,738 --> 00:21:12,797
到底怎么回事？碟刹在硬刹时会碎吗？
What was it?
The discs shattered under hard?

375
00:21:12,874 --> 00:21:15,604
这事总在赛道上发生，不过看过的人都知道，
It's always on tracks,
but anybody who's watched it,

376
00:21:15,677 --> 00:21:20,171
他们说只是车尾的速度在几秒内爆炸了。
they say it's just the speed from
right that end of the car in, like, seconds.

377
00:21:20,248 --> 00:21:21,215
是啊。
Yeah.

378
00:21:21,282 --> 00:21:23,807
他们倒觉得更像是爆炸而不是火灾。
It's more, they reckon,
an explosion than an a fire.

379
00:21:25,019 --> 00:21:27,010
所以，这招管用吗？
So, did this work?

380
00:21:28,556 --> 00:21:29,523
不行。
No.

381
00:21:30,458 --> 00:21:35,395
不过没关系，因为我们有阿尔法，简直太棒了。
But it didn't matter, because we had Alfas
and they were fantastic.

382
00:21:40,401 --> 00:21:45,065
哇，这操控…简直惊艳。真的找不到别的形容词。
Oh, that handling is... spectacular.
No other word for it, really.

383
00:21:46,507 --> 00:21:49,408
这车天生想让你开，想被开。
It wants you to drive it.
It wants to be driven, this car.

384
00:21:49,477 --> 00:21:52,139
看看它冲进这个弯时的气势。
Look at the vigor
with which it attacks this bend.

385
00:21:58,519 --> 00:22:01,215
连哈蒙德都在找好的一面。
Even Hammond
was looking on the bright side.

386
00:22:02,156 --> 00:22:04,784
它的重量刚好一千公斤多点。
It weighs just over 1,000 kilos.

387
00:22:04,859 --> 00:22:07,760
我的莲花Elise稍微不到一千公斤
My Lotus Elise weighs
just under 1,000 kilos

388
00:22:07,829 --> 00:22:09,694
所以…这就是莲花Elise。
so... it's a Lotus Elise.

389
00:22:14,669 --> 00:22:16,796
尽管我们热情高涨，
Despite our enthusiasm, though,

390
00:22:16,871 --> 00:22:19,135
但我们还是没有超过任何人。
we still hadn't overtaken anyone.

391
00:22:20,007 --> 00:22:21,770
哦，我的助力转向失灵了。
Oh, I've lost power steering.

392
00:22:22,844 --> 00:22:26,371
75号车也开始出现阿尔法综合症了。
And the 75
was starting to suffer from Alfa-itis.

393
00:22:27,215 --> 00:22:29,183
当你把手臂搭在中控台上
When you put your arm
on the center console

394
00:22:29,250 --> 00:22:32,378
你的手肘会把后窗给开下来，这可不太好。
your elbow does operate
the rear windows. That is an issue.

395
00:22:32,453 --> 00:22:36,856
不过它仍然拥有那种说不清的阿尔法魔力。
But it still has that Alfa magic
you can't ever really describe.

396
00:22:36,924 --> 00:22:39,017
只有阿尔法车主才懂。
Only Alfa Romeo owners know.

397
00:22:40,728 --> 00:22:42,923
那是什么声音？
What was that?

398
00:22:43,531 --> 00:22:46,295
哦，出了大问题。
Oh. Something's horribly wrong here.

399
00:22:46,367 --> 00:22:49,131
有种嗡嗡声，感觉怪怪的。
There's a buzz, there's a feel
that's different and odd.

400
00:22:50,271 --> 00:22:52,205
我只能进维修站了。
I had to make a pit stop.

401
00:22:52,840 --> 00:22:54,603
这件事你得记着
This is the thing you have to remember

402
00:22:54,675 --> 00:22:58,975
Alfa的目标是把车做到极致……简单说。
is Alfa build a car
to be as good as a car can be... briefly.

403
00:23:00,548 --> 00:23:03,949
于是就交给我的同事们来为Alfa的声誉撑腰了。
That left it up to my colleagues
to defend Alfa's reputation.

404
00:23:06,020 --> 00:23:07,578
哦——！
Oooh!

405
00:23:09,357 --> 00:23:12,451
把动力逼出来，冲过那条长弯道。
Squeeze the power
through the long-banked curve.

406
00:23:17,765 --> 00:23:18,857
剪辑。
Edit.

407
00:23:22,003 --> 00:23:25,461
我的飞轮轴承声音糟透了。
My flywheel bearings
sounded very poorly.

408
00:23:25,540 --> 00:23:29,306
换上新的轴承是个异常……嗯……复杂的活。
It's an incredibly erm... complex job
to put a new one in.

409
00:23:30,678 --> 00:23:33,169
现在是上午十点四十五分。
It's now quarter to 11 in the morning.

410
00:23:33,247 --> 00:23:37,343
如果我有的话，我大概能在……呃……
I might be able to get a new one in,
if I had one, by about erm...

411
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:41,311
……大约十月份左右吧。
...by about October.

412
00:23:43,291 --> 00:23:46,419
于是我决定用灭火器把它降温。
I therefore decided to cool it down
with a fire extinguisher.

413
00:23:46,494 --> 00:23:48,587
这主意真是妙极了。
It was a brilliant idea.

414
00:23:48,663 --> 00:23:51,427
但随后我从收音机里听到一条坏消息。
But then I got some bad news
over the radio.

415
00:23:52,333 --> 00:23:55,131
刚收到一条相当有意思的消息。
I've just been told something
rather interesting.

416
00:23:55,636 --> 00:23:57,297
有什么有意思的？
What's interesting?

417
00:23:57,371 --> 00:23:58,838
当你坐在维修区时，
While you're sitting in the pit,

418
00:23:58,906 --> 00:24:02,364
每一辆车穿过维修道墙都算一次超车。
every car that passes the pit lane wall
counts as an overtake.

419
00:24:02,443 --> 00:24:04,843
天啊，快点把千斤顶弄好行不行？
Oh, for God's sake.
Can we hurry up with that jack?

420
00:24:04,912 --> 00:24:08,905
更重要的是，Jezza，你一直被我甩在后面。
More to the point, Jezza, you're being
overtaken by me, consistently.

421
00:24:17,158 --> 00:24:19,126
又一次把你超过去，Jeremy。
Just overtaking you again, Jeremy.

422
00:24:19,627 --> 00:24:21,254
闭嘴，哈蒙德。
Shut up, Hammond.

423
00:24:25,299 --> 00:24:28,132
我的飞轮是今天遇到的第一个真正麻烦，
My flywheel was the first real problem
of the day,

424
00:24:28,202 --> 00:24:31,262
但紧接着问题接踵而至。
but soon they were coming thick and fast.

425
00:24:32,373 --> 00:24:33,340
离合器。
Clutch.

426
00:24:33,407 --> 00:24:35,967
我得去车库。刹车已经烂得不行。
I'm going to the floor.
The brakes have just cooked.

427
00:24:36,043 --> 00:24:38,944
我想我就在这儿休息，让刹车冷却一下。
I think I'll just rest here,
let my brakes cool for a bit.

428
00:24:39,013 --> 00:24:41,982
- 我的刹车完蛋了。
- 这味道真糟。
- My brakes are shot.
- This is smelling bad.

429
00:24:42,049 --> 00:24:45,280
驾驶座右侧已经垮了。
The driver's seat has collapsed
on the right-hand side.

430
00:24:45,353 --> 00:24:47,719
是水泵垫圈失效，还是哪儿出……
Is that water-pump gasket failure
or some sort of...

431
00:24:47,788 --> 00:24:49,221
- 是泵。
- 真正的泵。
- It's the pump.
- The actual pump.

432
00:24:50,491 --> 00:24:54,359
于是我想通过超越慢慢队长来赢得积分。
Then I tried to get a point
by overtaking Captain Slow.

433
00:24:58,332 --> 00:25:03,167
自然，这把我们给黑旗了，但起码我全盘承担。
Naturally, that got us black-flagged,
but at least I took full responsibility.

434
00:25:03,237 --> 00:25:04,534
- 你……
- 那是规矩。
- You...
- That's the rules.

435
00:25:04,605 --> 00:25:05,902
...倒向我这边。
- 胡说。
...turned in on me.
- Rubbish.

436
00:25:05,973 --> 00:25:07,565
那儿才是该转弯的地方。
That's where you're supposed to turn.

437
00:25:09,110 --> 00:25:13,171
更糟的是，超车挑战简直成了闹剧。
0n top of all this, the overtaking challenge
was descending into a farce.

438
00:25:14,949 --> 00:25:16,473
哎呀。
Oops.

439
00:25:16,550 --> 00:25:18,780
那是个刚把我甩开的16岁小子。
That's a 16-year-old boy
who's just overtaken me.

440
00:25:19,520 --> 00:25:20,646
开的是科萨。
In a Corsa.

441
00:25:24,926 --> 00:25:25,915
操！
Cock!

442
00:25:28,296 --> 00:25:31,129
我要抢一辆 Gallardo Superleggera！
I'm gonna take a Gallardo Superleggera!

443
00:25:31,866 --> 00:25:33,561
耶——！
Ye-e-e-s!

444
00:25:34,302 --> 00:25:36,930
简直爽翻！哦等下，他又跑了。
Utter joy! Oh, wait, now he's gone again.

445
00:25:38,005 --> 00:25:41,031
不过没过多久，我的失望更大了。
Soon, though,
my disappointment got worse.

446
00:25:43,945 --> 00:25:45,469
这可不妙。到底怎么了？
That's not good. What's happened?

447
00:25:46,213 --> 00:25:48,613
杰里米的排气管好像掉了。
Jeremy's exhaust
appears to have fallen off.

448
00:25:50,952 --> 00:25:53,580
这又让我被黑旗扣了分……
That got me black-flagged... again.

449
00:25:56,424 --> 00:25:58,654
啊——天呐！
Ho-o-oly cow!

450
00:25:58,726 --> 00:26:01,627
别担心，就是排气管嘛。
There's nothing to worry about.
It's just the exhaust.

451
00:26:01,696 --> 00:26:04,494
是阿尔法的车。他们干的事，你根本准备不好。
It's Alfas. They do things
that you're just not ready for.

452
00:26:04,565 --> 00:26:08,126
这点随后马上被证明了。
A point that was proved moments later.

453
00:26:09,971 --> 00:26:11,939
- 怎么了？  
- 离合器。
- What's the matter?
- Clutch.

454
00:26:12,006 --> 00:26:15,066
Well, get it back up,
otherwise the producers will laugh at us.
Well, get it back up,
otherwise the producers will laugh at us.

455
00:26:15,142 --> 00:26:16,268
我知道。
I know.

456
00:26:17,411 --> 00:26:19,038
来吧。
Come on.

457
00:26:19,814 --> 00:26:21,782
我简直不敢相信。
I can hardly believe this.

458
00:26:21,849 --> 00:26:25,580
现在现场唯一还能跑的车，就是哈蒙德的。
The only car that is out there
right now, working, is Hammond's.

459
00:26:27,455 --> 00:26:29,582
好吧，我说的“还能跑”……
Well, when I say "working"...

460
00:26:30,324 --> 00:26:32,292
把那根气缸还给我吧。
Please give me another cylinder back.

461
00:26:32,360 --> 00:26:35,796
拜托改回想法，重新变成四缸车啊。
Please change your mind back
and be a four-cylinder again.

462
00:26:38,632 --> 00:26:40,827
在我们把小毛病弄清楚后，
As we sorted out
our little niggles,

463
00:26:40,901 --> 00:26:43,096
成绩单继续往上爬。
the tally continued to mount.

464
00:26:43,170 --> 00:26:47,004
但连杰里米都承认，速度不是全部。
But even Jeremy was admitting
speed isn't everything.

465
00:26:47,074 --> 00:26:49,668
- 被超得多吗？  
- 那可是凯特哈姆和保时捷啊……
- Been overtaken much?
- There's Caterhams and Porsches...

466
00:26:49,744 --> 00:26:52,076
- 我得说，它们确实快。  
- 对，飞快。
- Can I just say? They're fast.
- Yeah, brisk.

467
00:26:52,146 --> 00:26:55,081
它们有灵魂、有性格、有激情吗？
Do they have the soul,
the character, the passion?

468
00:26:55,149 --> 00:26:56,912
如果凯瑟琳·罗斯——
If Katharine Ross -

469
00:26:56,984 --> 00:26:59,885
她出演《荒野大镖客》&《日落骑士》以及《毕业生》——
she of Butch Cassidy & The Sundance Kid
fame, and The Graduate -

470
00:26:59,954 --> 00:27:02,445
要是她来到这里挑最爱的车，
were to come here
and choose her favorite car,

471
00:27:02,523 --> 00:27:04,081
- 肯定不会选这些。  
- 不会。
- it would be none of those.
- No.

472
00:27:05,059 --> 00:27:07,527
终于，我们准备好重新上场了。
Finally, we were ready
to get back out there.

473
00:27:10,698 --> 00:27:12,928
而这次我们还有了计划。
And this time we had a plan.

474
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:16,868
齐心协力，我们要终结超车大屠杀。
By working together,
we'd stop the overtaking massacre.

475
00:27:17,805 --> 00:27:20,365
快跟上我，尽可能快。
Get alongside me, quick as you can.

476
00:27:22,376 --> 00:27:25,607
好，让他们来超我们吧。哈哈！
Yeah, now let's see 'em overtake. Ha-ha!

477
00:27:25,679 --> 00:27:28,409
太赞了！我们怎么没早想出来？
Brilliant!
Why didn't we think of this before?

478
00:27:34,789 --> 00:27:37,690
- 最近被超了吗？  
- 其实好久没了。
- Have you been overtaken recently?
- No, not for a while, actually.

479
00:27:37,758 --> 00:27:39,521
我也没有。
No, neither have I.

480
00:27:42,596 --> 00:27:46,828
当然，要阻止有人在宽阔路段偷偷超车，
Of course, to stop anyone
sneaking by on the wider bits of the track,

481
00:27:46,901 --> 00:27:49,131
我们得绕点儿过去。
we had to weave about a bit.

482
00:27:49,203 --> 00:27:51,637
哎呀，根本不顺。
Oh, that's not gone well.

483
00:27:51,705 --> 00:27:54,936
整体来看，我的战术简直完美。
0verall, though, my tactic
was working brilliantly.

484
00:27:55,009 --> 00:27:57,637
直到我被暗算。
Until I was stabbed in the back.

485
00:27:58,446 --> 00:28:00,573
- 这可是给我加分啊！
- 喂。
- That's a point for me!
- Oi.

486
00:28:04,485 --> 00:28:06,043
他们把比赛搞砸了。瞧瞧这情况。
They've ruined the game. Now look.

487
00:28:07,822 --> 00:28:11,223
背后捅刀的哈蒙德现在得意忘形了。
Back-stabber Hammond
was now getting very cocky.

488
00:28:14,095 --> 00:28:15,494
他摔下来了！
He fell off!

489
00:28:15,563 --> 00:28:17,360
哦，不！
Oh, no!

490
00:28:18,132 --> 00:28:19,463
哦，不！
Oh, no!

491
00:28:19,533 --> 00:28:21,330
噢，我的车没发动机了。
Oh, I've got no engine.

492
00:28:21,402 --> 00:28:24,633
布鲁特斯·哈蒙德的水泵坏了，出局。
Brutus Hammond
was out with a broken water-pump

493
00:28:24,705 --> 00:28:28,004
接着轮到卡修斯·梅了。
and then it was the turn of Cassius May.

494
00:28:29,410 --> 00:28:30,434
没有离合！
No clutch!

495
00:28:33,013 --> 00:28:35,607
与此同时，我这边情况相当不错。
Meanwhile, for me,
things were looking good.

496
00:28:36,884 --> 00:28:40,376
嘿，看起来我们这儿抓了个慢吞吞的家伙。
Hey, it looks like we got ourselves
a slowcoach here.

497
00:28:40,454 --> 00:28:42,513
我要开福克斯。
I'm gonna take the Focus.

498
00:28:43,290 --> 00:28:46,521
来吧！来吧，阿尔法！让全世界看看！
Come on! Come on, Alfa!
Show the world!

499
00:28:46,594 --> 00:28:50,428
是啊，小子，你现在感觉咋样？
Yeah, youth, how do you feel now?

500
00:28:50,498 --> 00:28:52,056
我得了分！
I've got a point!

501
00:28:52,133 --> 00:28:54,158
天啊，刹车！
Oh, my God, the brakes.

502
00:28:54,768 --> 00:28:55,757
哇！
Whoa!

503
00:28:57,338 --> 00:29:00,000
- 你的怎么了？
- 水全喷出来了。
- What's wrong with yours?
- All the water's coming out.

504
00:29:00,074 --> 00:29:01,507
- 真是吗？
- 这可不行。
- Is it?
- It's not good.

505
00:29:01,575 --> 00:29:03,975
- 杰里米怎么样？这就是关键。
- 我不知道。
- How's Jeremy doing? That's the thing.
- I dunno.

506
00:29:04,044 --> 00:29:06,035
其实，直接问他吧。
Ask him, actually.

507
00:29:06,113 --> 00:29:09,879
- 杰里米，你咋样？
- 不怎么好。
- Jeremy, how are you doing?
- Not brilliantly.

508
00:29:12,153 --> 00:29:14,121
我觉得还能凑合。
I think it's gonna be all right.

509
00:29:15,156 --> 00:29:17,488
我只需要辆拖车。
I just need a tow-truck.

510
00:29:17,558 --> 00:29:21,358
你觉得他们是会同情，还是会来捣蛋？
Do you think they're A, going to be
sympathetic or B, be a couple of?

511
00:29:21,428 --> 00:29:24,261
- 干得好！
- 不，他们要来捣蛋。
- Nice work!
- No, they're going to be a couple of.

512
00:29:24,331 --> 00:29:26,265
- 我跟你说发生了啥。
- 我说啊。
- I'll tell you what happened.
- I'll tell you.

513
00:29:26,333 --> 00:29:28,528
不，是有个人趁我不注意把它推倒了。
No, a man came and pushed it over
when I wasn't looking.

514
00:29:28,602 --> 00:29:31,332
- 不，你撞的，车都翻了。
- 我没撞。
- No. You crashed it and it's on its side.
- I didn't crash it.

515
00:29:32,973 --> 00:29:34,907
不，看看你整的啥玩意儿，兄弟！
No, look what you've done, man!

516
00:29:37,144 --> 00:29:39,339
- 对！
- 看看你搞的！
- Yeah!
- Look what you've done!

517
00:29:39,413 --> 00:29:41,745
这就是点小刮痕。
It's a minor scuff.

518
00:29:41,815 --> 00:29:43,874
来吧，车别掉链子。
Come on, car, don't let me down.

519
00:29:43,951 --> 00:29:46,442
啊……
Ahh...

520
00:29:48,556 --> 00:29:50,524
听起来这车不
太妙。
Doesn't sound good, that car.

521
00:29:54,295 --> 00:29:56,286
阿尔法根本杀不死。
You can't kill an Alfa.

522
00:29:57,198 --> 00:29:59,325
75号车更是杀不掉，绝对的。
You can't kill a 75, that's for sure.

523
00:30:00,234 --> 00:30:03,294
总之，看，我们现在已经回到
演播室里了。
Anyway, look, we've now come back
into the studio

524
00:30:03,370 --> 00:30:05,201
因为我们又有新挑战了。
because we've got another challenge.

525
00:30:05,272 --> 00:30:08,002
是啊。我们每个人被要求做一本
日历。
Yeah. We were each told
to make a calendar

526
00:30:08,075 --> 00:30:10,373
把自己的爱车摆进去，跟这些一样，
featuring our cars,
a bit like any of these,

527
00:30:10,444 --> 00:30:15,347
然后在西伦敦的顶级报刊亭挂个价0.54.99
卖。
and then put it on sale for 0„54.99
at a top West London newsagent's.

528
00:30:15,416 --> 00:30:17,816
每卖出一本日历我们就得一分。
We'd get one point
for every calendar we sold.

529
00:30:17,885 --> 00:30:20,046
好吧，我可是做了不少调研的，行吧？
Now, I did quite a lot of research, OK?

530
00:30:20,120 --> 00:30:22,486
我发现，决定日历销量的关键是…
And I discovered
that what makes a calendar sell...

531
00:30:22,556 --> 00:30:24,148
我这儿都有了，看看。
I've got them here. Look.

532
00:30:24,225 --> 00:30:26,819
看有什么共通点？干草堆。干草堆。
See what's in common?
Haystack. Haystacks.

533
00:30:26,894 --> 00:30:28,452
干草堆。
Haystacks.

534
00:30:29,630 --> 00:30:31,723
姑娘。还有…
Girl. And...

535
00:30:31,799 --> 00:30:35,667
于是我决定，我能做到的最好的事…就是这个！
So I decided the best thing I could do...
was this!

536
00:30:35,736 --> 00:30:38,603
等…等一下，那车是在干草堆后面吗？
Wh... Hang on. Is that the car
behind the haystack?

537
00:30:38,672 --> 00:30:40,037
是的。
Yes.

538
00:30:40,107 --> 00:30:43,941
因为我意识到，这75号根本不是阿尔法史上最漂亮的车，所以…
Cos I realized the 75 is not the prettiest car
Alfa ever made, so...

539
00:30:44,011 --> 00:30:45,979
我知道干草堆很受欢迎，于是我就这么做了。
I know haystacks are popular, so I did that.

540
00:30:46,046 --> 00:30:48,640
好了，看看，这就是你们放在货架上的日历。
Well, look, here is your calendar
on the shelf.

541
00:30:48,716 --> 00:30:51,981
- 那卖了多久？  
- 已经卖了一个月了。
- How long was that on sale for?
- It's been on sale now for a month.

542
00:30:52,052 --> 00:30:55,021
- 那卖了几本？  
- 零本，一个都没卖。
- Right, and how many have you sold?
- None. Not one.

543
00:30:55,089 --> 00:30:56,317
詹姆斯，你这结果咋样？
James, how have you done?

544
00:30:56,390 --> 00:31:00,258
我决定，我想找个非常漂亮的妹子和我的车一起拍日历封面。
I decided that I wanted a really nice woman
to pose with my car for the calendar.

545
00:31:00,327 --> 00:31:03,728
于是，我……给一些超模写信。
So, what I did was...
wrote to some supermodels.

546
00:31:03,797 --> 00:31:04,991
哪些超模？
What supermodels?

547
00:31:05,065 --> 00:31:08,660
凯特·莫斯、索菲·达尔，全部。那些大牌的。
Kate Moss, Sophie Dahl, the lot.
The big ones.

548
00:31:08,736 --> 00:31:11,034
- 有几个人回信？  
- 一个也没有。
- And how many replied?
- None.

549
00:31:11,105 --> 00:31:12,538
那你后面干嘛了？
So, what did you do?

550
00:31:12,606 --> 00:31:14,836
时间有点紧，我也急得慌
Well, time was getting a bit short
and I was desperate

551
00:31:14,908 --> 00:31:17,240
于是我打给了本地一家模特经纪公司…
so I rang up a local modeling agency...

552
00:31:17,311 --> 00:31:19,745
- 在哈默史密斯？  
- 对，我们这儿有。
- What, in Hammersmith?
- Yes. We've got one.

553
00:31:19,813 --> 00:31:23,749
我说，“能不能赶紧给我找个模特？我急着要一个来拍车日历。”
I said, "Could you send a model round?
I need one urgently for a car calendar."

554
00:31:23,817 --> 00:31:25,682
- 行。  
- 他们给了。
- Yes.
- And they did.

555
00:31:27,454 --> 00:31:29,251
詹姆斯，那是个男人。
James, that is a man.

556
00:31:29,323 --> 00:31:30,915
- 那是个男人。  
- 我知道！
- That is a man.
- I know!

557
00:31:31,692 --> 00:31:34,627
但我还能怎么办？他来了，挺兴奋地想要一展身手。
But what could I do? He turned up,
he was excited about his big moment.

558
00:31:34,695 --> 00:31:36,322
我可不能把他赶走，对吧？
I couldn't send him away, could I?

559
00:31:36,397 --> 00:31:38,228
- 卖了几本？  
- 零本。
- How many have you sold?
- None.

560
00:31:38,299 --> 00:31:39,664
好。
Right.

561
00:31:39,733 --> 00:31:41,963
- 那么……全靠你了……
- 是啊，好吧……
- So... it's all down to you...
- Yes, well...

562
00:31:42,036 --> 00:31:43,503
- …为了捍卫阿尔法的荣誉。
- 正是如此。
...to defend Alfa's honor.
- It is.

563
00:31:43,570 --> 00:31:47,666
- 我自以为机灵，决定想要
- 把我的车拍成一张动作照，挂在日历上
I was clever. I decided I wanted
an action shot of my car for my calendar

564
00:31:47,741 --> 00:31:50,232
- 但得自己动手，所以……
- 好啦，我现在就在这儿干。
but we had to do it ourselves so...
Well, here I am doing it.

565
00:31:50,311 --> 00:31:54,008
- 我给相机设了自带计时器。这
- 给了我十秒冲向车子，
I set the self-timer on the camera. That
gave me ten seconds to run to the car,

566
00:31:54,081 --> 00:31:58,177
- 上车、点火、冲过去，还想拍
- 车子飞驰的画面，可是我错过了。
get in, start it, drive past and get
a shot of the car moving, but I missed it.

567
00:31:58,252 --> 00:32:03,451
- 那我把计时延长，这样
- 给我更多时间冲过去、上车、开走
So I set it for longer, which gave me
more time to run to the car, get in, drive off

568
00:32:03,524 --> 00:32:05,492
- 然后……又错过了。
and then... I missed it again.

569
00:32:05,559 --> 00:32:10,189
- 然后我想，“如果我换个位置
- 把车开得离镜头更近”
So then I thought, "If I change the line
and drive the car closer to the lens

570
00:32:10,264 --> 00:32:14,064
- “我就能拍到车子近景
- 动感模糊的瞬间，冲过去的画面。”
"I'll get a close-up shot of it
all blurry in action as it went past."

571
00:32:14,134 --> 00:32:16,159
- 可是……呃……那…那也不太顺。
