847
00:46:41,634 --> 00:46:43,329
重新给我的座位套上覆盖物，简直太棒了。
Re-covering my seat, it's brilliant.

848
00:46:43,403 --> 00:46:45,462
- 用什么？
- 你的外套。
- Out of what?
- Your jacket.

849
00:46:45,538 --> 00:46:47,506
- 你！那是我的外套！
- 嗯。
- You! That is my jacket!
- Yeah.

850
00:46:50,610 --> 00:46:54,307
说实话，我有点失望，结果是这样。前部。
I am a bit disappointed, I must confess,
in how that's turned out. The front.

851
00:46:54,380 --> 00:46:57,816
侧面和其他都看起来不错，但前脸，简直太糟了。
The sides and everything look good,
but the front, it's very bad.

852
00:46:59,552 --> 00:47:01,782
为了转移评委对糟糕质量的注意，
To distract the judges
from the poor quality,

853
00:47:01,854 --> 00:47:05,551
我决定装上些非原装的赛车条纹。
I decided to go for
some non-original racing stripes.

854
00:47:06,326 --> 00:47:11,764
我还要跟组织者说，这可是厄瓜多尔的国家赛车颜色。
And I'm gonna tell the organizers these are
the national racing colors of Ecuador.

855
00:47:15,435 --> 00:47:17,995
夜幕降临时，一切进展顺利。
As night fell,
things were going well.

856
00:47:18,071 --> 00:47:21,063
车子开始看起来像新出厂的一样。
The cars were beginning to look
factory-fresh.

857
00:47:21,908 --> 00:47:25,173
是的，詹姆斯。詹姆斯，我做的东西居然管用。
Yes. James.
James, something I've done works.

858
00:47:25,245 --> 00:47:27,611
嗯，而且完美贴合。
Yeah, and it fits perfectly.

859
00:47:27,680 --> 00:47:29,944
不过，我有个大问题——
I, however, had one big problem -

860
00:47:30,016 --> 00:47:32,382
我的水泵仍然坏着，
my water-pump was still broken,

861
00:47:32,452 --> 00:47:35,944
这意味着我得手动给发动机加冷却液，
which meant I'd have to feed coolant
to the engine manually

862
00:47:36,022 --> 00:47:38,013
边开车边加。
as I was driving along.

863
00:47:38,758 --> 00:47:41,249
- 引擎盖怎么打开？
- 我还没搞清楚呢。
- How does the bonnet go down?
- I haven't worked that out yet.

864
00:47:41,327 --> 00:47:42,851
别催我，这可是工程活儿。
Don't rush me. This is engineering.

865
00:47:42,929 --> 00:47:44,954
要是我们用锯子在引擎盖上切个口子呢？
What if we make a cut-out in the bonnet
with a saw?

866
00:47:45,031 --> 00:47:46,999
他们会注意到的。
They'll notice that.

867
00:47:47,066 --> 00:47:50,558
你觉得他们会注意到吗，乘客座位上放着这个的情况下？
D'you think they'll notice that,
with this in the passenger seat?

868
00:47:54,807 --> 00:47:57,640
第二天早上，我们踏上了80英里的旅程
The next morning,
we set out on our 80-mile journey

869
00:47:57,710 --> 00:47:59,678
去参加展厅比赛。
to the concourse competition.

870
00:48:03,449 --> 00:48:07,783
这天的赛道真把我那可怜的75号车折腾坏了。
The track day
really had taken its toll on my poor 75.

871
00:48:08,988 --> 00:48:13,049
好吧，我的发电机故障指示灯、刹车故障指示灯亮了，
OK, I've got an alternator-failure
warning light, brake-failure warning light,

872
00:48:13,126 --> 00:48:15,321
油压警示灯也亮起
oil-pressure warning light

873
00:48:15,395 --> 00:48:18,592
还有那破碎变速箱的明显噪音。
and the unmistakable sound
of a ruined gearbox.

874
00:48:20,066 --> 00:48:22,193
这就是我喜欢阿尔法的原因。
And that's what I like about Alfas.

875
00:48:22,268 --> 00:48:25,897
世上没有其他阿尔法今天会出现这么多问题。
No other Alfa in the world
has all these problems... today.

876
00:48:25,972 --> 00:48:27,633
它们有别的故障。
They have different ones.

877
00:48:29,142 --> 00:48:31,235
比如理查德的车。
Take Richard's car, for example.

878
00:48:32,679 --> 00:48:35,341
从人体工学来看，我觉得这套系统有点儿缺陷。
Ergonomically, I think this system
is a little flawed.

879
00:48:35,415 --> 00:48:38,441
把手可以更顺手一点儿。
The handle could
fall a little more easily to hand.

880
00:48:39,686 --> 00:48:43,816
然后詹姆斯也想争辩说他有问题。
Then James tried to argue
that he had a problem, too.

881
00:48:43,890 --> 00:48:45,187
- 哈蒙德。
- 什么事？
- Hammond.
- Yes?

882
00:48:45,258 --> 00:48:47,920
我的暖气卡在最大档，根本关不掉。
My heater's stuck in the fully-on position.

883
00:48:47,994 --> 00:48:51,987
说实话，兄弟，这根本算不上最糟的状况。
That's not the worst problem
it could have, really, mate, if I'm honest.

884
00:48:59,872 --> 00:49:03,137
在下一次维修停顿时，理查德和我决定给詹姆斯
At the next repair halt,
Richard and I decided to show James

885
00:49:03,209 --> 00:49:05,575
看看真正的麻烦到底长啥样。
what a real problem might be like.

886
00:49:05,645 --> 00:49:07,010
噢，嗬嗬！
Ooh hoo-hoo!

887
00:49:07,080 --> 00:49:09,548
- 想要成熟点的么？
- 我想要超成熟的。
- Would you like the mature?
- I'm thinking extra mature.

888
00:49:09,615 --> 00:49:11,207
- 各来一份。
- 那太棒了。
- One of each.
- That's brilliant.

889
00:49:13,453 --> 00:49:15,478
那味儿儿肯定够呛。
That's gonna smell poor.

890
00:49:16,356 --> 00:49:18,187
给他那通风口盖上。
Cover his vent.

891
00:49:18,257 --> 00:49:20,555
这玩意儿其实就是个巨型刨丝器。
It's actually just a huge cheese-grater, this.

892
00:49:20,626 --> 00:49:22,753
他来了，快点，快点。
He's coming, he's coming. Quick. Quick.

893
00:49:23,930 --> 00:49:25,727
- 什么？
- 请别碰车。
- What?
- Hands off car, please.

894
00:49:25,798 --> 00:49:27,356
抱歉。
Sorry.

895
00:49:30,470 --> 00:49:34,270
重回路上，我们的老马匹再次累积里程。
Back on the road,
our old war horses racked up the miles.

896
00:49:36,676 --> 00:49:38,337
我们现在要驶向福斯路。
We're coming up now to the Fosse Way.

897
00:49:41,314 --> 00:49:43,441
我想不出还有比这更爽的事了
I can think of few greater pleasures

898
00:49:43,516 --> 00:49:48,783
就是开着一辆赛道条纹的阿尔法·罗密欧在这条路上飞驰。
than driving an Alfa Romeo
with racing stripes on this road.

899
00:49:49,789 --> 00:49:52,417
可惜，我和大家的乐子
Sadly, though, my fun and everyone else's

900
00:49:52,492 --> 00:49:55,552
被詹姆斯抢了风头，有点扫兴。
was spoiled a bit
because James was in front.

901
00:50:02,635 --> 00:50:05,126
哈蒙德的车怎么还能跑？
How is Hammond's car still working?

902
00:50:05,905 --> 00:50:07,372
这下子保住了。
This is gonna make it.

903
00:50:08,975 --> 00:50:12,001
你们看见没？阿尔法简直是魔法般的存在，宛如巫师。
You see? Alfas are magic.
They're like wizards.

904
00:50:12,078 --> 00:50:14,239
可是接着就干了这事儿。
But then this happened.

905
00:50:15,047 --> 00:50:16,412
啊！
Agh!

906
00:50:16,482 --> 00:50:19,042
啊！完蛋了。
Agh! That's a disaster.

907
00:50:19,118 --> 00:50:21,814
那水泵的把手给掉了。
The handle's come off his water-pump.

908
00:50:24,824 --> 00:50:27,292
然后又出了乱子。
And then this happened.

909
00:50:27,360 --> 00:50:29,828
哦……什么？
Oh... what?

910
00:50:30,596 --> 00:50:32,860
不要现在！快点。
No, not now! Come on.

911
00:50:33,833 --> 00:50:35,130
哎呀，着火了。
Oh, it's on fire.

912
00:50:35,201 --> 00:50:40,537
正常在《Top Gear》，我们有句座右铭：“朋友摔倒就别扶了。”
Now, normally on Top Gear, our
motto is, "If a friend falls, leave him there."

913
00:50:40,606 --> 00:50:44,474
可今天我们联手对抗制片人，
But because today
we were united against our producers,

914
00:50:44,544 --> 00:50:46,512
詹姆斯竟然回来救我。
James came back to rescue me.

915
00:50:47,747 --> 00:50:49,374
好吧，这不对劲。
Well, that's not right.

916
00:50:50,883 --> 00:50:52,373
哈蒙德。
Hammond.

917
00:50:52,452 --> 00:50:55,250
我被救了，连车都没坏。
I have been rescued
and I haven't even broken down.

918
00:50:55,321 --> 00:50:56,413
嗨。
Hello.

919
00:50:58,691 --> 00:51:01,285
因为詹姆斯的车状态极佳，
Because James's car was in the best nick,

920
00:51:01,360 --> 00:51:03,351
他得把哈蒙德拖走。
he would have to tow Hammond.

921
00:51:04,330 --> 00:51:06,525
谢谢把车拽回来，兄弟。
真的很感激。
Thanks for the tow, mate.
I appreciate it, really I do.

922
00:51:06,599 --> 00:51:07,725
没事儿，别客气。
That's quite all right.

923
00:51:08,835 --> 00:51:10,700
对不起。对不起。
Sorry. Sorry.

924
00:51:10,770 --> 00:51:11,759
哈蒙德！
Hammond!

925
00:51:15,441 --> 00:51:17,409
开始在环形交叉口减速了。
Beginning to slow for the roundabout.

926
00:51:17,477 --> 00:51:19,104
把松弛的空间给填上。
Taking up slack.

927
00:51:19,178 --> 00:51:23,046
- 140码。
- 把松弛补上。补上了。
- 140 yards.
- Got the slack. Got the slack.

928
00:51:23,115 --> 00:51:24,776
哎呀！抱歉。
Ooh! Sorry.

929
00:51:24,851 --> 00:51:26,819
抱歉，抱歉。我…哎呀。
Sorry, sorry. I... Ooh.

930
00:51:26,886 --> 00:51:29,480
抱歉，兄弟。我在找车灯开关。
Sorry, mate. I was looking for
my headlight switch.

931
00:51:29,555 --> 00:51:30,852
我真的一点儿也找不到它在哪儿。
I really don't know where it is.

932
00:51:31,624 --> 00:51:33,251
什么？不行！兄弟！
What? No! Mate!

933
00:51:35,628 --> 00:51:37,926
- 发生什么事了？
- 什么？
- What's happening?
- What?

934
00:51:37,997 --> 00:51:39,988
他还弄坏了东西。
He's broken something, as well.

935
00:51:41,968 --> 00:51:43,765
他把我甩了。
He left me.

936
00:51:43,836 --> 00:51:45,804
- 介意吗？
- 我不行。听着。
- Would you mind?
- I can't. Listen.

937
00:51:45,872 --> 00:51:47,931
嗯…可是…
Well... But...

938
00:51:48,774 --> 00:51:51,800
- 可你不能把阿尔法甩在后面。
- 痛！
- But you can't leave an Alfa behind.
- Ow!

939
00:51:51,878 --> 00:51:56,747
于是那辆已经死掉的车只能被那辆快要挂掉的车给拽走。
So the car that was dead had to be towed
by the car that was dying.

940
00:51:56,816 --> 00:51:58,408
噢，听这声音。
Oh, listen to that now.

941
00:51:59,952 --> 00:52:02,921
这声音怪得像是车在叫。
That's a weird noise
for a car to make.

942
00:52:04,190 --> 00:52:07,421
- 好多了。你干了什么？
- 我挂二挡。
- That's better. What have you done?
- I've gone into second.

943
00:52:07,493 --> 00:52:09,688
二挡挺好用的，常被低估。
Second's nice. It's underrated as a gear.

944
00:52:13,132 --> 00:52:14,861
我的天啊。
Oh, my God.

945
00:52:14,934 --> 00:52:18,199
从那以后一路顺坡。
From then on, it was downhill all the way.

946
00:52:18,271 --> 00:52:20,603
除了我们在上坡的时候。
Except when we were going uphill.

947
00:52:20,673 --> 00:52:23,198
哈蒙德…
Hammond...

948
00:52:23,276 --> 00:52:26,143
…爬坡时情况不妙。
...it's not going well up the hill.

949
00:52:29,982 --> 00:52:32,712
它来了，背着战场上的兄弟
Here it is,
carrying its mate from the battlefield

950
00:52:32,785 --> 00:52:35,845
虽然它一条腿都断了。
even though one of its legs is shot off.

951
00:52:35,922 --> 00:52:39,289
而梅下士直接弃船而去。
While Corporal May just abandoned ship.

952
00:52:40,860 --> 00:52:44,523
倒是好笑，梅为逃跑付出了代价。
Happily, though, May was paying the price
for his desertion.

953
00:52:51,404 --> 00:52:53,463
这味道根本不像发动机的味儿。
That doesn't smell like the engine.

954
00:52:58,477 --> 00:53:00,342
看着不错，时髦。
Looking good. Stylish.

955
00:53:14,716 --> 00:53:16,013
奶酪火锅？
Fondue?

956
00:53:21,822 --> 00:53:24,313
尽管我的仪表全被打得稀巴烂，
Despite my bearings being shot to bits,

957
00:53:24,392 --> 00:53:26,792
我们已经快到过夜点了。
we were now near the overnight halt.

958
00:53:34,068 --> 00:53:37,435
- 我不敢相信。真的不敢相信。
- 我的车？
- I don't believe it. I do not believe it.
- My car?

959
00:53:37,505 --> 00:53:41,737
那辆疲惫的老意大利车居然把坏掉的同伴拽了回来…
That tired old Italian car
has towed its broken mate...

960
00:53:43,978 --> 00:53:45,946
詹姆斯看到我们可不太高兴。
James wasn't very pleased to see us.

961
00:53:46,013 --> 00:53:49,574
- 他到底摧毁了多少？
- 好吧，他把车牌子给打掉了。
- How much damage has he done?
- Well, he's knocked the number plate off.

962
00:53:49,650 --> 00:53:53,017
- 嗯，还不至于太烂。
- 可比之前更糟了……
- Well, it's not that bad.
- It's worse than it was...

963
00:53:53,087 --> 00:53:54,987
- 你可以把这边抛光掉。
...今天早上。
- You could buff that out.
...this morning.

964
00:53:55,056 --> 00:53:57,217
- 看看它把他的弄成啥样了。
- 对我的影响更大。
- Look what it's done to his.
- It's done more to mine.

965
00:53:58,025 --> 00:54:01,483
其实，你……我应该对你发火。
看看你干了什么。
Actually, you... I should be cross at you.
Look what you've done.

966
00:54:01,562 --> 00:54:03,029
- 我怎么会这么干？
- 看。
- How could I have done that?
- Look.

967
00:54:03,097 --> 00:54:04,587
你在后面。
You were behind.

968
00:54:06,767 --> 00:54:08,860
星期天。展厅日。
Sunday. Concourse day.

969
00:54:08,936 --> 00:54:13,635
赛道上挤满了
一些有史以来最棒的车手的座驾。
And the fields were filling with
some of the best drivers' cars ever made.

970
00:54:13,708 --> 00:54:15,938
...阿尔法·罗密欧展区...
...the Alfa Romeo concourse...

971
00:54:16,010 --> 00:54:19,070
这些车子被一遍遍
吸尘、除尘、抛光
All of which were being hoovered
and dusted and polished

972
00:54:19,146 --> 00:54:21,944
然后又一次
吸尘、除尘、抛光。
and then hoovered
and dusted and polished again.

973
00:54:22,917 --> 00:54:25,385
与此同时，路上几英里外…
Meanwhile, a few miles down the road...

974
00:54:26,754 --> 00:54:29,746
- 我来第二轮，你准备好了吗？
- 哎哟呀！
- I'm going for a second. Are you ready?
- Aaaghhhh!

975
00:54:32,493 --> 00:54:34,859
可悲的是，詹姆斯今天早上没法拖理查德。
Sadly, James is not able to tow Richard
this morning.

976
00:54:34,929 --> 00:54:37,159
他仍然因为昨天的事闷闷不乐。
He's still in a bit of a mood over yesterday.

977
00:54:38,065 --> 00:54:40,397
不过，还有个更大的问题，
There was a bigger issue, though,

978
00:54:40,468 --> 00:54:43,733
因为规则规定所有汽车必须靠自己发动机到达。
because the rules say all cars
must arrive under their own steam.

979
00:54:44,472 --> 00:54:47,407
于是，在门口外，我们把车拦了下来…
So, just outside the gates,
we pulled over...

980
00:54:47,475 --> 00:54:48,806
机会百出。
There's every chance.

981
00:54:48,876 --> 00:54:51,242
...哈蒙德胆大地打电话求助。
...and Hammond bravely rang for help.

982
00:54:51,312 --> 00:54:53,837
来吧。现场！现场！现场！
Come on. Live. Live. Live.

983
00:54:53,914 --> 00:54:57,179
- 哦，那车真漂亮，老GTV。
- 嗯，真的很赞。
- Oh, that's a pretty car, the old GTV.
- Yeah, that is lovely.

984
00:54:58,552 --> 00:55:00,144
来吧。来吧。来吧。
Come on. Come on. Come on.

985
00:55:00,221 --> 00:55:03,349
不，你这家伙买了辆菲亚特，兄弟。
你根本没抓住要点……
No, you've just bought a Fiat, mate.
You haven't got the idea...

986
00:55:04,258 --> 00:55:05,691
开始！
Begin!

987
00:55:08,162 --> 00:55:10,130
现在！
Now!

988
00:55:12,867 --> 00:55:14,528
这事毫无希望。
It was hopeless.

989
00:55:16,170 --> 00:55:18,695
于是我们想出了个办法。
So we came up with a plan.

990
00:55:18,772 --> 00:55:23,175
詹姆斯同意拖理查德，
而我的车负责藏绳子。
James agreed to tow Richard,
and my car would hide the rope.

991
00:55:24,445 --> 00:55:26,777
“那事故到底是怎么闹的，克拉克森先生？”
"And how did the accident happen,
Mr. Clarkson?"

992
00:55:27,948 --> 00:55:31,850
在入口处我们必须紧紧靠在一起，
来骗过裁判员。
At the entrance we had to bunch right up
to fool the marshals.

993
00:55:32,753 --> 00:55:36,245
我们总是一起出行，如果你不介意我们粘在一块，
那就太好了。
We always travel together, so if you don't
mind us sticking together that'd be kind.

994
00:55:37,424 --> 00:55:39,119
早上好。
Morning.

995
00:55:40,494 --> 00:55:42,462
- 不，这里没有拖绳。
- 没什么好看的。
No, no tow-ropes here.
Nothing to see here.

996
00:55:44,498 --> 00:55:46,227
门口有几个裁判员。
There are some marshals at the gate.

997
00:55:46,300 --> 00:55:48,894
我们得装作若无其事，
穿过去。
We need to move past them
as if everything is normal.

998
00:55:48,969 --> 00:55:50,300
- 在左边。
- 在右边…（原文未完）
- Up on the left.
- Up on the I...

999
00:55:53,507 --> 00:55:56,374
- 早安。
- 在右边，靠近……（原文未完）
- Morning.
- Over on the right, next to the...

1000
00:55:56,443 --> 00:55:58,240
抱歉。抱歉。
Sorry. Sorry.

1001
00:55:58,312 --> 00:56:00,337
悄悄地…
Very discreetly...

1002
00:56:00,414 --> 00:56:01,381
哦……
Oh...

1003
00:56:03,017 --> 00:56:07,647
……我们悄悄把车开到评审区，停在竞争对手中间。
...we made our way to the judging area
and parked amongst our rivals.

1004
00:56:09,823 --> 00:56:12,485
- 我们在竞争。
- 对，没错。呃……
- We're competing.
- Yeah. Yeah. Erm...

1005
00:56:12,560 --> 00:56:16,519
作为……一个……上帝的男人
As... a man... of God

1006
00:56:16,597 --> 00:56:19,725
我想，你要是我把钥匙塞进去，你肯定会不爽吧。
you'd take it badly, I'm assuming,
if I were to, for instance, key it.

1007
00:56:19,800 --> 00:56:23,201
很快评委们就冲向我们的车了。
Soon the judges
descended on our cars.

1008
00:56:23,270 --> 00:56:26,398
我们得给它们打个分。你能打开引擎盖吗？
We've got some serious marking to do.
Would you be able to open the bonnet?

1009
00:56:26,473 --> 00:56:27,531
- 不能。
- 不能。
- No.
- No.

1010
00:56:27,608 --> 00:56:29,576
我想让你记住——
What I want you to put in your mind -

1011
00:56:29,643 --> 00:56:32,737
那引擎盖下是一件光鲜亮丽的完美标本。
under that bonnet
is a burnished specimen of perfection.

1012
00:56:32,813 --> 00:56:34,246
- 那就是零分。
- 零。
- So that's zero.
- Naught.

1013
00:56:34,315 --> 00:56:35,873
- 你的车漆……
- 对。
- Your paintwork...
- Yes.

1014
00:56:35,950 --> 00:56:39,078
大部分颜色和出厂时一模一样。
Most of it is the same color
that it came out the factory.

1015
00:56:39,153 --> 00:56:41,485
- 正是如此。
- 那我给它……算了，打两分吧。
- It is.
- So I've given it er... two points for that.

1016
00:56:41,555 --> 00:56:43,182
- 满分是？
- 15分。
- Out of?
- 15.

1017
00:56:43,257 --> 00:56:44,224
两分？
Two?

1018
00:56:44,291 --> 00:56:47,317
不不不，发动机还在里面。还有啥要检查的？
No, no, we keep the engine in there.
Anything else you need to check?

1019
00:56:47,394 --> 00:56:48,725
- 就这样吗？
- 呃，后备箱。
- Is that it?
- Er, boot.

1020
00:56:48,796 --> 00:56:50,263
对，就在下面。
Yes, it's down there.

1021
00:56:53,834 --> 00:56:56,132
- 换挡时会咔嗒响吗？
- 不会。
- Does it clunk when you change gear?
- No.

1022
00:56:56,203 --> 00:56:58,501
我……我稍微给这个补了点。
I... I did patch this one slightly.

1023
00:56:58,572 --> 00:57:01,598
- 我倒没动，我找了个软垫工来弄的。
- 好的。
- Well, I didn't. I had an upholsterer do it.
- Right.

1024
00:57:01,675 --> 00:57:04,439
- 你有原装工具箱吗？
- 有。
- Do you have the original toolkit?
- Yes.

1025
00:57:04,511 --> 00:57:05,876
- 能给我看看吗？
- 不行。
- Can you show it to me?
- No.

1026
00:57:05,946 --> 00:57:09,347
不能因为这个奶酪扣分。
我可没把它放那儿。
You can't deduct marks for the cheese.
I didn't put it there.

1027
00:57:09,416 --> 00:57:11,748
- 你该把它清理干净啊。
- 那就算八分吧。
- You should have cleaned it off.
- So let's call it eight.

1028
00:57:11,819 --> 00:57:13,286
嗯。
Yeah.

1029
00:57:13,354 --> 00:57:15,322
- 你写了“七”。
- 对。
- You've written "seven".
- Yeah.

1030
00:57:16,190 --> 00:57:19,023
评委们退场去算分了。
The judges retired
to tot up the scores.

1031
00:57:19,093 --> 00:57:21,926
但说实话，我们早已经是赢家了。
But truth be told,
we were already winners.

1032
00:57:23,597 --> 00:57:25,929
你们看，要是我们开的是三辆普通车的话
You see, if we'd been in three normal cars

1033
00:57:26,000 --> 00:57:28,560
这一路只能算是中部的普通兜风。
this would have been
a drive across the Midlands.

1034
00:57:30,437 --> 00:57:34,203
但这三台老古董把它变成了一场冒险。
But these three old crocks
had turned it into an adventure.

1035
00:57:35,075 --> 00:57:39,171
笑声、失误、友情、回忆、刺激。
Laughter, mishaps,
friendship, memories, thrills.

1036
00:57:41,115 --> 00:57:43,913
这才是油腔滑调的天堂。
That is petrol head heaven.

1037
00:57:43,984 --> 00:57:45,246
哈蒙德！
Hammond!

1038
00:57:45,319 --> 00:57:47,378
而且，正如我们一直所说，
And, as we've always maintained,

1039
00:57:47,454 --> 00:57:51,686
唯一能开到那儿的办法……就是坐阿尔法·罗密欧。
the only way you can get there...
is in an Alfa Romeo.

1040
00:57:59,066 --> 00:58:01,500
- 我们说对了。
- 想要一台吗。
- We were right.
- Want one.

1041
00:58:01,568 --> 00:58:03,559
心里说，我想要一个。
Heart says I want one.

1042
00:58:03,637 --> 00:58:07,368
好了，现在该去拿评委的分数了。
Anyway, it is now time to get the scores
from the judges.

1043
00:58:07,441 --> 00:58:11,571
——詹姆斯，你得了几分？  
——满分150… 74分。
- James, what did you get?
- Out of a possible 150... 74.

1044
00:58:11,645 --> 00:58:15,172
74分，差不多算及格了。
74. That's nearly a pass.

1045
00:58:15,249 --> 00:58:18,047
而我… 23.5分。
Now, I got... 23 and a half.

1046
00:58:18,118 --> 00:58:21,485
是啊，这是最低分
Yeah. Which was the lowest score

1047
00:58:21,555 --> 00:58:24,888
在全场历史上有史以来的最低分。
ever recorded in er... concourse history.

1048
00:58:24,958 --> 00:58:27,017
是啊，直到我出现为止。
Yeah. Until I came along.

1049
00:58:27,895 --> 00:58:29,726
——你得了几分？  
——我得了9分。
- What did you get?
- I got nine.

1050
00:58:32,032 --> 00:58:33,522
——9分？  
——9分。
- Nine?
- Nine.

1051
00:58:33,600 --> 00:58:36,068
9分。好了，来看看总成绩。
Nine points. So, here we go.
These are the totals.

1052
00:58:36,136 --> 00:58:39,628
詹姆斯，你负… 129.5分。
James, you are minus... 129 and a half.

1053
00:58:39,707 --> 00:58:41,470
——对——  
129.5分。
- Yep.
- 129 and a half.

1054
00:58:41,542 --> 00:58:45,842
——理查德，你负169分。  
——是的，我是。
- Richard, you are minus 169.
- Yes, I am.

1055
00:58:45,913 --> 00:58:50,543
而我负127.5分！
And I'm minus 127 and a half!

1056
00:58:51,318 --> 00:58:55,584
所以，自从三年前的廉价车挑战之后，
And so, for the first time since the
cheap-car challenge about three years ago,

1057
00:58:55,656 --> 00:58:58,648
我居然真的赢了点东西！
I've actually won something!

1058
00:58:58,726 --> 00:59:00,956
干得漂亮。
Well done.

1059
00:59:01,028 --> 00:59:03,121
——更好的是——  
—— 为什么？
- And it gets better.
- Why?

1060
00:59:03,197 --> 00:59:08,829
因为，作为奖品，制作人说你可以把那75分（车）留下
Because, as a prize, the producers
have said you get to keep that 75

1061
00:59:08,902 --> 00:59:11,530
并且整整一年都当你的车。
and use it as your car for a whole year.

1062
00:59:11,605 --> 00:59:14,836
还有啊，你知道吗？说实话，身为汽车爱好者
And d'you know something?
Honestly, as a car lover

1063
00:59:14,908 --> 00:59:17,069
我真找不到比这更想要的了。
I can't think of anything I'd like more.

1064
00:59:17,144 --> 00:59:19,977
呃… 所以我们该结束啦，非常感谢观看。
Er... so that's time to end now.
Thank you very much for watching.

1065
00:59:20,047 --> 00:59:21,344
下周见，晚安。
See you next week. Good night.

1066
00:59:21,368 --> 00:59:26,368
